items: extension-name-collision v3-a-toplevel-extension-shadows-a-given-instance-one-of-the-same-name
paths: file:v3/src/Lower.scala file:v3/BUGS.md
scope: |
  A top-level `extension` and a `given`-instance `extension` of the same name collide, and the
  top-level one wins whatever the receiver is. Reproduced in fourteen lines (in the entry), and it
  is what blocks `std-monaderror`, `std-index` and — through them — the withheld arm of
  `v3-given-instance-as-a-receiver-is-refused`. One defect, three positions.

  THE MECHANISM IS ORDER, NOT A MISSING TABLE. `rewriteExtensionCalls` rewrites `x.m(args)` to
  `m(x, args)` whenever `m` is a top-level def name that is not a class member or a builtin — no
  look at the receiver at all — and a top-level `extension [A](fa: Either[String, A]) def
  handleError` lifts to exactly such a def. It runs BEFORE `rewriteGivenExtensionCalls` in the
  pipeline, so it eats the call before the resolver that CAN type the receiver ever sees it:

      rewriteGivenExtensionCalls(rewriteExtensionCalls(resolveMethodRefs(…)))

  THE FIX IS TO SWAP THE TWO, so the pass that knows the receiver's type claims what it can and the
  name-only rewrite takes the rest. That is "the more specific wins", which is the rule the subtrait
  preference already encodes one level down.

  IT NEEDS NO NEW GUARD, and that is checked rather than hoped: `instanceOnly` — the set whose
  members trigger the refusal — already subtracts `defs.map(_.name)`, so a method that a top-level
  extension also provides is NOT instance-only and cannot be refused by the resolver running first.
  On an `Either` receiver `pick` returns None, no refusal fires, the expression falls through
  unchanged, and `rewriteExtensionCalls` handles it in the second pass.

  MEASUREMENT: N with floors DIFF 3 / CRASH 9; the fourteen-line reproducer must print `Some(4)`;
  `std-monaderror` and `std-index` read INDIVIDUALLY. A swap of two passes is exactly the kind of
  change that moves something far away, so the gates matter more than usual here — and `front-gate`,
  `exec-gate` and `front-diff` are ALREADY red on `opaque-type`, someone else's fixture landing
  ahead of its parser support, so those three must be compared against a control rather than read.
next: swap the two passes, probe the reproducer, measure
